{"path":"cpp/ranges/drop_view/size.html","id":"ref-51f3b502480508db","name":"std::ranges::drop_view<V>::size","declarations":[{"code":"constexpr auto size()\n    requires ranges::sized_range<V>;","notes":"(since C++20)","since":"20","until":null},{"code":"constexpr auto size() const\n    requires ranges::sized_range<const V>;","notes":"(since C++20)","since":"20","until":null}],"headers":["ranges"],"intro":"Returns the number of elements.\n\nLet base_ be the underlying view, count_ be the stored count (the number passed to the constructor, or 0 if *this is default constructed). Equivalent to:\n\nconst auto s = ranges::size(base_);\nconst auto c = static_cast<decltype(s)>(count_);\nreturn s < c ? 0 : s - c;","sections":[{"title":"Parameters","text":"(none)"},{"title":"Return value","text":"The number of elements."}],"examples":[{"code":"#include <array>\n#include <ranges>\n\nint main() {\n    constexpr std::array a{42, 43, 44};\n    static_assert(std::ranges::drop_view{std::views::all(a), 0}.size() == 3);\n    static_assert(std::ranges::drop_view{std::views::all(a), 1}.size() == 2);\n    static_assert(std::ranges::drop_view{std::views::all(a), 2}.size() == 1);\n    static_assert(std::ranges::drop_view{std::views::all(a), 3}.size() == 0);\n    static_assert(std::ranges::drop_view{std::views::all(a), 4}.size() == 0);\n}","output":null,"outputKind":"Behavior demonstrated in code","unicodeEscaped":false}],"summary":"Returns the number of elements.","source":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view/size","introduced":"20","removed":null}
